203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Solar energy has become one of the fastest-growing renewable energy sources worldwide, with large-scale photovoltaic \(PV\) installations now common in both utility and residential settings. However, PV systems are exposed to electrical and environmental stresses over time, which can cause faults that reduce efficiency and, in severe cases, pose fire or safety risks. Early and automated fault detection is therefore essential for maintaining system reliability and maximizing energy output.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (This project presents a machine learning-based diagnostic system that classifies the operating condition of a PV system using real sensor measurements. The system is trained on a large, publicly available PV fault dataset containing over 1.37 million labelled observations collected from two PV strings, covering five operating conditions: Normal, Short Circuit, Degradation, Open Circuit, and Shadowing. Each observation includes electrical readings \(string voltages vdc1, vdc2 and currents idc1, idc2\) and environmental readings \(irradiance irr and module temperature pvt\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
